{"error":{"data":{"error":{"code":"invalid_api_key","message":"Incorrect API key provided: Sk-proj-********************************************************************************************************************************************************-SsA. You can find your API key at https://platform.openai.com/account/api-keys.","param":null,"type":"invalid_request_error"}},"isRetryable":false,"name":"AI_APICallError","requestBodyValues":{"input":[{"content":[{"text":"You are a news intelligence assistant. Create a comprehensive, well-structured markdown report based on the analysis below.\n\nUser Query: \"Basketball\"\n\nAnalysis Data:\n=== NEWS ARTICLES ===\n[1] Michigan State basketball dominates North Carolina in Fort Myers (USA Today)\nMichigan State dominates North Carolina in Fort Myers in Thanksgiving affair\nURL: https://spartanswire.usatoday.com/story/sports/college/spartans/mens-basketball/2025/11/27/michigan-state-basketball-dominates-north-carolina-in-fort-myers/87500868007/\n[2] Yates scores 25, Diallo adds 19 to lead Washington past Nevada 83-66 in Acrisure classic (Yahoo Entertainment)\nWesley Yates III scored 17 of his 25 points in the second half after Zoom Diallo had 13 of his 19 in the first half and Washington beat Nevada 83-66 in the Acrisure Holiday Classic on Thursday. The Huskies (5-1), who won their bracket in the same tournament l…\nURL: https://sports.yahoo.com/articles/yates-scores-25-diallo-adds-000628920.html\n[3] UNC Basketball suffers first loss against #11 Michigan State (Tar Heel Blog)\nAn impressive second half performance from the Spartans doomed Hubert Davis’ squad.\nURL: https://www.tarheelblog.com/unc-basketball/49613/unc-basketball-final-score-michigan-state\n[4] Ogbole sets career highs with 21 points, 13 boards and Rutgers beats UNLV to end Players Era tourney (Yahoo Entertainment)\nEmmanuel Ogbole set career highs with 21 points and 13 rebounds, Dylan Grant added 17 points and eight rebounds, and Rutgers ended a three-game losing streak...\nURL: https://sports.yahoo.com/articles/ogbole-sets-career-highs-21-000414888.html\n[5] JJ Redick on how new Lakers forward Drew Timme can contribute (USA Today)\nCould new Lakers forward Drew Timme have a bit of untapped potential?\nURL: https://lebronwire.usatoday.com/story/sports/nba/2025/11/27/jj-redick-on-how-new-lakers-forward-drew-timme-can-contribute/87500559007/\n[6] Michigan State Beats North Carolina, 74-58 (The Only Colors)\nSpartans stay perfect and pick up another win on a ranked opponent.\nURL: https://www.theonlycolors.com/basketball/43495/michigan-state-beats-north-carolina-74-58\n[7] COLUMN: For the love of the game and the end of an era: A special thank you for my time at the Times (Timeswv.com)\nThe greatest college basketball coach of all time, Mike Krzyzewski, once said, “Your heart has to be in whatever you lead. I’ve never made a decision based on what will get me the most money. It was what was going to give me the most happiness.” After a year …\nURL: https://www.timeswv.com/opinion/columns/column-for-the-love-of-the-game-and-the-end-of-an-era-a-special/article_33dbbc70-fe11-4a62-b2d4-6c8fa653ce39.html\n[8] Thursday Headlines: Happy Thanksgiving! (A Sea Of Blue)\nHappy Thanksgiving to everyone in the BBN!\nURL: https://www.aseaofblue.com/kentucky-wildcats-news/154518/thursday-headlines-happy-thanksgiving-edition\n[9] JVNDB-2025-020403:campcodes の Retro Basketball Shoes Online Store in PHP MySQL における SQL インジェクションの脆弱性 (Jpcert.or.jp)\n\nURL: http://vrda.jpcert.or.jp/feed/ja/JVNiPedia_JVNDB-2025-020403_AD_1.html\n[10] JVNDB-2025-020402:campcodes の Retro Basketball Shoes Online Store in PHP MySQL におけるクロスサイトスクリプティングの脆弱性 (Jpcert.or.jp)\n\nURL: http://vrda.jpcert.or.jp/feed/ja/JVNiPedia_JVNDB-2025-020402_AD_1.html\n[11] Israel opens World Cup qualifying campaign with tough tests vs. Germany, Croatia (The Jerusalem Post)\n“We are about to launch the next campaign that is very significant for Israeli basketball and for all of us,” noted Beit Halachmi. “It’s a very big challenge, but also a huge opportunity.\nURL: https://www.jpost.com/israel-news/sports/article-876441\n[12] Euroleague returns to Israel after vote, home games resume (The Jerusalem Post)\nEuroleague basketball is returning to Israel in December, with games set to resume at Menora Mivtachim Arena and Jerusalem’s Pais Arena. After more than two years of hosting games abroad, Euroleague and EuroCup basketball will return to Israel following a una…\nURL: https://www.jpost.com/israel-news/sports/article-876492\n[13] 29.5\" Franklin Indoor/Outdoor Official Size Hard Court Basketball w/ Pump $8.99 + Free Shipping w/ Prime or on $35+ (Slickdeals.net)\nAmazon [amazon.com] has 29.5\" Franklin Indoor/Outdoor Official Size Hard Court Basketball w/ Pump for $8.99. Shipping is free w/ Prime or on $35+.\n\n\nProduct Description from Amazon:The Hard Court\nURL: https://slickdeals.net/f/18888379-29-5-franklin-indoor-outdoor-official-size-hard-court-basketball-w-pump-8-99-free-shipping-w-prime-or-on-35\n[14] Takeaways from No. 7 Maryland women’s basketball’s 95-38 win over Hofstra (Testudo Times)\nThe Terps led by 20 in the first quarter.\nURL: https://www.testudotimes.com/maryland-terps-womens-basketball/85917/takeaways-from-no-7-maryland-womens-basketballs-95-38-win-over-hofstra\n[15] \"I ate and drank all summer\" - Michael Jordan on how he spent the summer of 1989 after falling to Pistons Bad Boys (Basketball Network)\nBulls icon Michael Jordan didn’t lock himself up in the gym after their heartbreaking loss to the Pistons.\nURL: https://www.basketballnetwork.net/old-school/i-ate-and-drank-all-summer-michael-jordan-on-how-he-spent-the-summer-of-1989-after-falling-to-pistons-bad-boys\n[16] Burglars raided Josh Hart's hotel room and stole a fortune in jewelry (Basketball Network)\nIn September, Josh Hart lost $185k worth of jewelry to a hotel burglary.\nURL: https://www.basketballnetwork.net/latest-news/burglars-raided-josh-harts-hotel-room-and-stole-a-fortune-in-jewelry\n[17] Brooks scores 21, Pierre grabs 21 boards and No. 25 N.C. State women top Green Bay 79-67 in Cancun (Yahoo Entertainment)\nZoe Brooks scored 21 points, Khamil Pierre had a career-high 21 rebounds and No. 25 N.C. State pulled away in the fourth quarter to defeat Green Bay 79-67 in the Cancun Classic on Thursday. Brooks and Pierre both had eight points in the final period when the …\nURL: https://sports.yahoo.com/articles/brooks-scores-21-pierre-grabs-230902658.html\n[18] Virginia Tech basketball: Hokies lose first game, fall to Saint Mary’s in Battle 4 Atlantis tourney (Gobblercountry.com)\nThe Hokies were without senior forward Tobi Lawal.\nURL: https://www.gobblercountry.com/virginia-tech-basketball/28950/virginia-tech-basketball-hokies-lose-saint-marys-battle-4-atlantis\n[19] Harding hits go-ahead jumper with 48 seconds left as TCU beats No. 10 Florida 84-80 (Yahoo Entertainment)\nBrock Harding made a go-ahead jumper in the key with 48 seconds left and then hit five free throws in the final 13 seconds for TCU, which rallied to stun No. 10 Florida 84-80 in the first game of the Rady Children's Invitational on Thursday. Jace Posey scored…\nURL: https://sports.yahoo.com/articles/harding-hits-ahead-jumper-48-230158573.html\n[20] 76ers guard Tyrese Maxey takes his handles to the National Dog Show (Yahoo Entertainment)\nPhiladelphia 76ers guard Tyrese Maxey has great handles on the basketball court. Though as he learned recently, that skill set isn’t transferrable to the dog-handling ring.\nURL: https://sports.yahoo.com/nba/article/76ers-guard-tyrese-maxey-takes-his-handles-to-the-national-dog-show-225840541.html\nTotal articles fetched: 68 from sources: newsapi, guardian, arxiv\n\n=== SENTIMENT ANALYSIS ===\nOverall Sentiment: neutral\nTrend: Balanced coverage\nTop article sentiments:\n- Article sentiment: neutral (score: 0.50, emotions: )\n- Article sentiment: neutral (score: 0.50, emotions: )\n- Article sentiment: neutral (score: 0.50, emotions: )\n- Article sentiment: neutral (score: 0.50, emotions: )\n- Article sentiment: neutral (score: 0.50, emotions: )\n\n=== TREND ANALYSIS ===\nTemporal Pattern: No temporal pattern data available\n\n=== BIAS ANALYSIS ===\nSource Diversity: 10 left-leaning, 0 right-leaning, 58 neutral (total: 68)\nRecommendation: Good balance of neutral sources. No significant biases detected in coverage\n\n=== PERSONALIZATION ===\n\nCreate a markdown report with the following structure:\n\n## Summary\n[2-3 sentence executive summary answering the user's query directly]\n\n## Key Findings\n[3-5 bullet points of the most important findings]\n\n## Latest News\n[List top 5-7 articles with titles, sources, and brief context. Include sentiment indicators where relevant]\n\n## Analysis & Insights\n[Combine insights from sentiment, trend, and bias analysis into a cohesive narrative]\n[Include sections like \"Trending Topics\", \"Sentiment Overview\", \"Source Diversity\" as appropriate]\n\n## Personalized Recommendations\n[If personalization data is available, include personalized insights and recommended follow-ups]\n\n## Sources\n[List all news sources used, grouped by provider]\n\nGuidelines:\n- Use **bold** for emphasis\n- Use proper markdown formatting (##, ###, -, *, etc.)\n- Be concise but informative\n- Cite specific articles and sources\n- Use neutral, professional tone\n- Include relevant URLs when available\n- Make it easy to scan with clear headings and bullet points\n- Synthesize information across agents rather than just listing their outputs\n- Highlight contrasts or agreements between different sources","type":"input_text"}],"role":"user"}],"model":"gpt-4o","temperature":0.7},"responseBody":"{\n  \"error\": {\n    \"message\": \"Incorrect API key provided: Sk-proj-********************************************************************************************************************************************************-SsA. You can find your API key at https://platfor